# dynatrace_credentials_v2 (Data Source)

-> **Dynatrace SaaS only**

-> This data source requires the OAuth permission **Read credential vault entries** (`credential-vault:entries:read`). With the additional permission `credential-vault:entries:admin`, entries owned by other users are listed as well.

The `dynatrace_credentials_v2` data source queries for credentials stored within the Credential Vault using the properties `name`, `type`, `scope` and `user`. All of them are optional; without any, all credentials are returned. `name` is matched case-insensitively. As credentials aren't unique by these properties, multiple credentials can be returned within `items`.

## Example Usage

```terraform
data "dynatrace_credentials_v2" "creds" {
  name = "Office365 Access Token"
  type = "TOKEN"
}

output "credential_ids" {
  value = data.dynatrace_credentials_v2.creds.items[*].id
}
```

